{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat tools/p10/README.md && cat docs/planning/reviews/C45/attempt-01/verdict.json'","aggregated_output":"# C45 / P10 explicit future verification\n\nP09 remains an immutable historical prerequisite. Its full source and originally\nignored evidence are archived under C45 activation; no old inventory or verdict\nis edited. C30/C41 owner standing remains distinct from independent scores.\n\n`seal.py` derives all current mapped native IDs plus C45's identity assertions\nand the approved 16 selected repository commands. `c45_baseline` uses the existing\nRust Runner, Manifest and Environment; it retains raw RunRecords and excludes\nsetup already performed offline, duplicate frontend execution and the two real\nlogin-Keychain/search-list probes. P10 selects C45 rather than replaying retired\nC01-C44 commands. Production FileStore/authority and disposable-file Keychain\nregressions replace old import/adoption and private-Keychain probes explicitly.\n\n`supervise.py` requires guest Terminal ancestry, a global UI-writer flock, sealed\nsource, exact fixture/bundle bindings and foreground checks. Every stage keeps\nraw stdout/stderr and the original runner/native records. It stops on failure\nand preserves completed stages. Partial stages require explicit ownership and\nraw-result diagnosis; model/tool exit does not terminate this Terminal-owned job.\n`native.py` only relocates existing driver evidence paths and uses their original\nassertions. `acceptance_c45.py --smoke` is a short current identity preflight,\nnever cumulative acceptance. The real C45 rows also require separate qualified\nproduction-interface and mapped coverage; UI absence is not non-adoption proof.\n\n`finalize.py` binds actual executions. `qualification.py` verifies complete ID\nmembership, approved command/cwd, original RunRecord/native results, input/log\nhashes and per-driver evidence. Exact reuse requires executable, complete bundle,\nrelevant helper closure, flags and conditions. Changed test/lint targets must\nexecute. Unaffected carry retains original artifacts and requires actual unchanged\ndependency-file proofs. No assertion retirement can be introduced by omission.\nP10 consumes the same qualified candidate without claiming new execution.\n\n`packet.py make|audit C45|P10 attempt-NN` uses a fresh read-only configured Codex\nreview through the retained launcher. Audits never assign scores. C45 can be\naccepted at 8 under D034, then needs actual full9 before P10; P10 needs actual\nfull9 with empty fixes/blockers/gaps. C26/P08 remains open/manual fallback.\n\nBoth release-candidate packaging and the actual production build entrypoint\nrequire C01-C25 plus genuine audited P09/P10 proof, including C45 full9 member and\nqualified coverage. C26 is not a circular prerequisite of its own release build.\nThis work authorizes no live product calls, user credential/data discovery,\npublication, signing, notarization or installation.\ncat: docs/planning/reviews/C45/attempt-01/verdict.json: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
