380,20 @@\n         \"id\": \"C44-N01\",\n         \"check\": \"One presentation (P09 closure): the fixture app's first run is the wizard with no Features rail and no 'Use the new interface' switch anywhere; after the tenant is set up, every destination the catalogue lists is opened from the Go menu (Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client, Administration; Runtime Security, AI Gateway and Red Team & Models opening Administration on their product; Sessions & Reports and Settings framed by the v2 shell (Import from v1 removed, D060)) under the v2 Destinations rail, each captured in light and dark at 1440\\u00d7900 as the whole-app screenshot set under evidence/C44/parity/app, with no plaintext secret and no learner chrome (outside Academy) in any destination's tree; \\u23182 opens the Inbox and \\u2318, Settings through the native menu; the built stylesheet carries the reduced-motion clamp; the bundle is Node-free and no Node, Bun or Deno process runs beside the app; after a quit and relaunch 15 s of startup open no internet socket from the app or its WebKit processes, Home shows with the tenant active and Administration reads with the kept client; every pre-P09 native assertion has its standing in evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md (exercised by a named v2 check, self-run through legacy_v2 \\u2014 C03, C04, C05, C06, C07, C10, C11, C24 \\u2014 ported into this check, or retired with its reason) and the mapped drivers' records on this bundle bind the gate: an exercised, self-run or ported assertion without a passing target fails this check.\"\n       }\n+    ],\n+    \"C45\": [\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"C45-N01\",\n+        \"check\": \"Prepared real fixture is Prisma AIRS Desktop Fixture1.0.0, identifierio.cdot.airs-desktop.fixture, binaryprisma-airs-desktop. Production config independently names Prisma AIRS Desktop1.0.0/io.cdot.airs-desktop. Native About/menu/title and Home-first catalogue agree; startup/settings/sessions focus and headings use the one presentation. Exact candidate process identity, executable and complete bundle are bound.\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"C45-N02\",\n+        \"check\": \"Fresh synthetic setup starts with the wizard and no adopted tenants, credentials, sessions or approvals. Controlled prior alpha/v2 root/service canaries remain byte-identical across setup/relaunch/reset. Old real application roots, login Keychain and live endpoints are never inspected. Namespace isolation and non-adoption require passing production-interface FileStore/authority and disposable-file Keychain regressions, not only absence of UI.\"\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"id\": \"C45-N03\",\n+        \"check\": \"No alternate presentation selector or alpha/tenant-profile/API-profile-adoption surface or native intent remains. Ordinary current-format collection open/create/import/editor behavior is retained, along with active Settings/Sessions/Diagnostics/Academy behavior and C44 scope/commit-phase guards. Every current mapped legacy/modern target is accounted by the same candidate baseline or explicit valid coverage proof; no assertion disappears via omission.\"\n+      }\n     ]\n   }\n }\ndiff --git a/docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md b/docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md\nindex 49e29cef..a3e73f16 100644\n--- a/docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md\n+++ b/docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md\n@@ -199,3 +199,7 @@ The active implementation task may deliver reviewed Git commits to the exact\n owner-specified remote using normal pushes. Application release publication,\n hosting changes, and promotion over v1 must remain within the owner's explicit\n release instruction; preparing a signed package does not by itself publish it.\n+\n+## P10 — C45: one presentation and fresh identity (D061/D062)\n+\n+After actual P09all9/audit, C45 implements C45-draft.md and chunks/C45.md. P10=[C45] must pass an actual cumulative independentall9 review before the signed C26/P08release. C26 itself is not required before its own release build; genuine P09/P10 proofs and existing C01–C25 prerequisites guard that production boundary. The approved manual review fallback remains explicit while C26/P08 is open; no controller receipts are fabricated. Verification follows verification-policy.md: one justified C45 baseline, affected followups and reuse for P10 when valid.\ndiff --git a/docs/planning/decisions.md b/docs/planning/decisions.md\nindex 9ed6ca76..c341ed31 100644\n--- a/docs/planning/decisions.md\n+++ b/docs/planning/decisions.md\n@@ -2508,3 +2508,11 @@ Decided by the owner on 2026-10-31, in the owner's words: \"i really really reall\n - Naming: this desktop becomes v1 and the previous one the alpha. The rename touches the application identity that lets the two coexist (bundle identifiers, data roots, Keychain namespaces, D001-era identities) and the whole document set; it is its own chunk after P09, not a find-and-replace.\n - The product name shown today stays \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2\" until that chunk.\n \n+\n+## D061 — One presentation and fresh application identity (C45/P10)\n+\n+Owner-approved2026-11-01 brief, activated after actual P09attempt02 all9/audit on2026-11-02. Prisma AIRS Desktop1.0.0 uses io.cdot.airs-desktop and fixtureio.cdot.airs-desktop.fixture (Prisma AIRS Desktop Fixture). Port maintained helpers/tests, remove legacy/variant/alpha/profile-adoption readers/contracts and start fresh without reading, migrating or deleting alpha/v2 data/credentials. Ordinary selected collection formats remain. C45 followsD034 acceptance then actualall9; P10 requires actual independentall9. P10 closes before signedC26/P08release. No publication/signing/notarization/installation or additional live scope.\n+\n+## D062 — Risk-based future verification and explicit evidence reuse\n+\n+Owner2026-11-02 policy in verification-policy.md applies toC45/P10/future tasks, never retroactively to sealed P09. Select checks from behavior/dependencies/boundary risk. One broad C45 identity/isolation/cleanup baseline is justified after focused/cross-consumer preflight; later fixes/merges andP10 execute affected checks and retain valid original evidence with exact-artifact proof or an honest unaffected-impact rationale. Every assertion/check is accounted; raw outcomes/artifact bindings remain immutable. New commits/worktrees/scores/fingerprints alone do not trigger full native/Rust repetition. Actual independent reviews and separate live/release gates remain.\ndiff --git a/docs/planning/review-protocol.md b/docs/planning/review-protocol.md\nindex bbb3ad27..5bea8b19 100644\n--- a/docs/planning/review-protocol.md\n+++ b/docs/planning/review-protocol.md\n@@ -136,3 +136,7 @@ from a successful CLI exit code or queue acknowledgement alone. It also rejects\n a verdict whose request ID or echoed fingerprints differ from the packet, a\n verdict for an expired attempt, and a phase completion lacking a passing phase\n review.\n+\n+## C45/P10 verification scheduling (owner decision, 2026-11-02)\n+\n+Use verification-policy.md and the candidate's small change-impact/verification-plan record. Current source is reviewed independently; a new score/attempt/source fingerprint alone does not schedule a full native or Rust rerun. One justified C45 identity/isolation/cleanup baseline can serve both chunk and P10 reviews. Follow-up fixes execute causal/affected checks. Required coverage is partitioned into current execution, exact proof reuse, honest unaffected carry, justified not-applicable or an actual explicit owner decision; missing/edited/failed proof is rejected. Original run/verdict/artifact bindings are immutable. Historical P09 and prior gate semantics stay unchanged. C26/P08 remains open with the approved fresh read-only review fallback; no controller completion is fabricated.\ndiff --git a/docs/planning/test-catalogue.md b/docs/planning/test-catalogue.md\nindex dd66a58b..c3cd968d 100644\n--- a/docs/planning/test-catalogue.md\n+++ b/docs/planning/test-catalogue.md\n@@ -25,8 +25,7 @@ separate evidence. Do not assert implementation-private structure for its own sa\n   credentials are separate. Deny wrong-origin redirects or custom endpoint\n   changes that would forward a credential without an explicitly reviewed new\n   destination binding. Preserve legitimate operator-reviewed endpoint overrides\n-  and explicitly selected nonsecret tenant-profile import; whitelist metadata,\n-  discard embedded secrets and never follow credential-file references.\n+  and ordinary user-selected current-format collection imports. Alpha/v2 tenant-profile readers and credential-file discovery are removed under D060/C45.\n   No implicit environment/tenant file\n   loading, upstream fallback, persistent renderer storage, or secret log fields.\n - **T06 Protected storage:** locked/denied/unavailable/corrupt store, interrupted\n@@ -65,7 +64,7 @@ separate evidence. Do not assert implementation-private structure for its own sa\n   consistent Home/Inbox source facts, and no false complete/zero/absent claims.\n - **T14 API Client documents:** edit/save/conflict while typing, invalid input,\n   environment/secret separation, import/path traversal/size errors, multipart,\n-  cookies/redirect auth, cancellation, history/download, Git/profile adoption,\n+  cookies/redirect auth, cancellation, history/download, read-only Git,\n   and recovery from interrupted writes. Arbitrary workbench targets cannot borrow\n   privileged application credentials through renderer-supplied references.\n - **T15 Harness process:** actual native binary and bounded bootstrap/JSONL\n@@ -85,10 +84,7 @@ separate evidence. Do not assert implementation-private structure for its own sa\n \n ## Import, quality, and artifacts\n \n-- **T18 Import transaction:** dry-run selection, versions/source lock, account\n-  match, protected source reads, malformed/oversized/traversal inputs, interruption\n-  at each commit point, restart, duplicate import, destination conflict, rollback,\n-  and source-byte preservation. No credentials/sessions/approvals transfer.\n+- **T18 Fresh setup and ordinary file isolation (C45/D060):** bootstrap in the new application/data/credential identities without reading, adopting, replaying or purging alpha/v2 stores. Synthetic old-root/service canaries survive new setup, restart and reset; old stores/vaults receive no reads. Ordinary user-selected API collection/cURL/Insomnia/case files retain their formats, bounded parsing, traversal refusal, reviewed selection and source-byte preservation. The former alpha transaction, tenant-profile import and API profile adoption are intentionally retired; historical results remain unchanged.\n - **T19 Diagnostics privacy:** seeded canary secrets and customer content absent\n   from logs/crash files/exports by default; explicit redacted export; correct\n   retention/reset; no analytics/crash upload attempts; encrypted user history\n@@ -141,3 +137,5 @@ Before review, challenge security-critical tests with a relevant deliberate\n behavior mutation or equivalent negative probe. Show that violating an invariant\n fails the test; do not create an exhaustive mutation framework or mirror every\n implementation detail. Run mutations only in isolated disposable copies.\n+\n+C45/P10 checks follow verification-policy.md: record affected behavior/dependencies, selected checks, retained original artifact bindings, uncertainty and the reason for any full baseline. One complete C45 identity/isolation/cleanup baseline is justified; follow-ups/merge/P10 reuse valid coverage with explicit proof or unchanged-impact rationale and execute affected targets. Every required assertion is accounted; no omission or score substitutes for evidence.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
