{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a new defect in C45’s release-proof consumer. Although it requests historical qualification with `current=False`, the nested reuse verifier still requires today’s source inventory to match the old seal. An in-memory probe reproduced rejection after an unrelated source entry was added, with all frozen evidence unchanged. This would block the intended later C26 work; it does not invalidate the recorded C45 baseline.\n"}}
